closures-autofix: skip-failed-recording -- THE REPAIR DID NOT HAPPEN.
No commit will be pushed, so waiting for one waits forever. This is
the case `.cursor/rules/ci-autofix.mdc` already lists as a human
judgment call, and its rule against re-recording an UNDER-SCOPED
yourself does not apply once the bot has reported that it did not.
A script exited non-zero WHILE being recorded, so its closure is only
what it reached before stopping -- and merging that would under-scope
the gate, which is why the merge refuses it. The under-approximation
this job was going to repair is real and still unrepaired.
Fix the failing script first; the closures job re-records on the next
push and this repair then happens on its own.

